===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|bar|Haferl}} {{lb|bar|West Central Bavarian|South Bavarian|Tyrol}}

===Etymology===
Diminutive of {{m|bar|Häfn}}, from {{inh|bar|gmh|haven}}, from {{inh|bar|goh|havan}}, {{m|goh|hafan}}. Probably related to {{m|bar|hebn}}, ultimately from {{inh|bar|gmw-pro|*habbjan}}.

===Pronuciation===
* {{IPA|bar|/ˈhe̞fɐl/}}

===Noun===
{{head|bar|noun|plural|Häferln}} {{lb|bar|East Central Bavarian|Vienna|South Bavarian|Carinthia}}

# [[mug]] {{gloss|[[cup]] for [[beverage]]s, usually having a [[handle]] and used without a [[saucer]]}}
# [[hothead]] {{gloss|one who angers easily}}
# {{lb|bar|sports|games|humorous}} [[trophy]], [[cup]] 

